# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep SECRETS and host-specific state out of it.
# Anything listed here is invisible to `docker build`, including to the `COPY . .` in the build stage.

# Secrets — never in an image. Configuration is supplied at `docker run` time.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Reinstalled inside the image by `npm ci`; copying the host's tree would also drag in
# platform-specific native binaries built for the host OS.
node_modules
.next
out

# Version control and editor state
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea

# Local tooling / agent state that the app never reads at runtime
.claude
.personas
docs/harness
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
bench
uat
tiger
kpi-sim
reference-data

# Build artifacts and logs
*.log
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
